# chip — BOTTOM-UP + BY-DEPTH LAYER CAPS: the chip-scale policy vehicle
# (docs/internal/hier_layer_caps.md §12/§13 Phase 5).  Same design and same
# bottom-up flow as chip_bottomup.buda (3x big2 + 3x mix2 + 100 top buses,
# 432 leaf blocks / 13320 nets, healerless for fast experimentation), with
# ONE extra line declaring the whole policy:
#
#   reserve_top_layers 2
#
# Counting DEEPEST-FIRST over intrinsic cell levels: the leaf cells (level 1,
# no interconnect of their own) get [lowest..M5], the big2/mix2 cell templates
# (level 2 — this is the band that bites, their cell-local buses) get
# [lowest..M9], and the top cell (level 3, past the argument list) stays
# UNRESTRICTED so the 100 cross-instance top buses keep M10/M11 to themselves.
# That is the BKM the whole feature exists to express, in one line instead of
# a set_cell_layer_cap per cell type.
#
# THE BAND MUST SCALE WITH THE STACK — which is why this vehicle says
# `reserve_top_layers 2` and not an absolute band.  It was originally
# written as `set_layer_caps_by_depth M3 M5` for the 6-layer stack, where
# [..M5] left M6/M7 (the top PAIR) to the top level.  The identical text on
# the 10-layer stack reserves SIX layers for a top level that needs two, and
# starves the cell templates: measured 3192 unplaced bits, against 1708 when
# the band is rescaled.  Measured alternatives on this stack, cell band:
# M5 -> 3192 unplaced, M7 -> 1898, M9 -> 1708, uncapped -> 1604.
# `reserve_top_layers 2` derives the M9 cap from the stack itself, so it
# stays correct if the stack grows again (byte-identical to the hand-written
# `set_layer_caps_by_depth M5 M9`: 358/1708/93).
#
# Note the leaf argument is a free choice here: the level-1 cells are true
# leaves with no cell-local bundles, so `M5 M9` and `M7 M9` produce byte-
# identical results.  Only the level-2 band bites in this design.
#
# The separation is visible in report_wirelength's per-layer breakdown: zero
# cell-template WL above M9, and M10/M11 exclusively top-level.  Compare
# against chip_bottomup.buda (identical but uncapped) for the §12 study.
source chip_tracks.buda
open_bdb chip.bdb.sql
set_bottom_up big2
set_bottom_up mix2
align_bottom_up
reserve_top_layers 2
derive_busterms 2
add_blocks_from_bdb 0
add_blocks_from_bdb 1 skip
add_blocks_from_bdb 2 skip
set_max_bundle_bits auto
run_hier_bundler depth 2
generate_hier_topologies
set_planner_param healersAhead 1
run_planner hier 5 signal_tracks
run_nuts
check_template_tracks on_mismatch independent
run_detailed_nuts
negotiate_congestion
report_wl
check_design
exit
